# Claude's desktop app writes here by default, and that default happens to
# land inside this repository.  On 18 Oct 2026 it held the Clipper study
# document - built from Clipper's copyrighted materials - untracked and
# unignored, in a PUBLIC repo, on the branch about to be pushed.  It had
# never been committed; it was one `git add -A` away from being published
# under Larry's name in the repo he had invited Clipper to read.
#
# This line stops the accident.  It does NOT make the folder safe: an
# ignore rule is bypassed by `git add -f`, and it does nothing for a zip,
# an archive, or a copy of the working tree.  Nothing from Clipper's
# materials belongs in this repository at all.
Claude outputs/

# The drill test harness drives a real browser through playwright, which
# is a dev dependency installed into the working tree.  19 MB of it, and
# it was untracked AND unignored in a public repo -- the same shape as the
# accident the rule above was written for.  package.json and
# package-lock.json ARE tracked, so the harness is reproducible: the
# version it was verified against is pinned, not whatever npm resolves on
# the day.
node_modules/
